Copilot's agent runtime identifies as an SDK host, not VS Code (ROADMAP P0-8).

VS Code's agent host sets GITHUB_COPILOT_INTEGRATION_ID=code-oss ("Identify
VS Code's agent host traffic in CAPI"). With Triage's own GitHub OAuth app
(patch 0004) that combination failed: the owner's Agents prompt got "Auto
couldn't pick a model: the routing service is unavailable" and no model list,
while the same prompt worked with VS Code's OAuth app. GitHub documents the
other combination for apps that embed the Copilot SDK: "You create a GitHub
OAuth App (or GitHub App), users authorize it, and you pass their access token
to the SDK. Copilot requests are made on behalf of each authenticated user,
using their Copilot subscription."
(docs.github.com/en/copilot/how-tos/copilot-sdk/setup/github-oauth)
So Triage no longer sets the integration id and the runtime keeps its own.

